e  aims to do so by stuffing her sword down  the back of her dress until it's time  for some stabbing  it's a great visual but it doesn't quite  hold up if you take a minute to think  about it with the number of people  taking second looks at diana as she  walks past  someone probably should have noticed she  was carrying a giant piece of magic  metal could they have seen the hilt of  the sword and simply thought it was  elaborate jewelry  sure but ludendorff probably should have  noticed something was up when he  literally put his hands on it  leftover weapons diana spends the film  convinced that all she has to do to stop  the war is kill ares but steve has a  different mission  his goal is the same but he's going  after general ludendorff and dr poison  who have manufactured extremely powerful  chemical  weapons the evil doctor didn't just make  the poison gas that will kill  untold numbers of people if it's  unleashed on the world though she also  granted ludendorff incredible strength  and durability which almost makes him  diana's equal in combat  almost at the end of the film aerys  tries to get diana to kill dr poison who  he considers the ultimate example of  humanity's corruption  diana spares her but her lab is  destroyed by steve and his team  and the poison gas is neutralized when  steve sacrifices his life to blow it all  up it all seems like a pretty tidy  ending  except that we know dr poison worked in  multiple places to perfect her formula  research like this tends to involve a  lot of documentation and it makes sense  that she'd even have earlier slightly  less deadly versions of both the poison  and the strength enhancer that we never  saw  even assuming she never made a chemical  weapon again after diana spared her  it's not hard to imagine dr poison's  creations or the science behind them  falling into the hands of the nazis just  a few years later  gods and monsters the film's climactic  showdown between diana and ares reveals  a twist  aries 